# Liveness double move of a ConsumeCallable: a `ConsumeCallable[..]` value is
# single-owner — calling it consumes it, so a second call is a double move.
# Mirrors production consume_callable_once_error.gg (E_DoubleMove).
# KNOWN-ORACLE-BUG: `ggdef run` currently under-rejects this (missing live->dead
# kill on a consume-call — filed ggdef track). Self-host + production are CORRECT to
# REJECT; do NOT change the self-host to match ggdef. Asserted vs the self-host driver.
void main():
    ConsumeCallable[int(int)] f = !(n): n * 2
    int r1 = f(5)
    int r2 = f(10)
    print(f"{r1}{r2}")
